+    // QWebEngine delivers cookieAdded asynchronously, so the SSO token cookie
+    // set on the 302 leading to the final page can arrive after the final URI
+    // has already been reported. openconnect decides "SSO done" on the report
+    // carrying the final URI and only uses the cookies of *that* report, so
+    // without this wait it would submit an empty token. Wait briefly for any
